#!/bin/bash
# claude-glm — Claude Code against one of the Anthropic-compatible providers in
# config/wolfmux/lib/providers.sh. One file; the name it is called by picks the row
# (the claude-fable precedent, ADR-0017):
#
#   claude-glm        -> GLM-5.3          claude-glm-flash -> GLM-5.3 Flash
#   claude-kimi       -> Kimi Code        claude-moonshot  -> Kimi K3 (open platform)
#   claude-deepseek   -> DeepSeek V4      claude-minimax   -> MiniMax M3
#   claude-qwen       -> Qwen 3.7 Plus
#
# The endpoint, the key and the model mapping exist ONLY inside this process. Nothing is
# written to ~/.claude/settings.json, the shell profile, or any file, so plain `claude`
# and `claude-fable` stay on the Claude subscription.
#
# The key is read from the macOS Keychain (service: see the provider's row).
#   helper (default)  Claude Code gets a command that reads the Keychain on demand.
#                     The key never enters the environment, so the agent's
#                     subprocesses, transcripts and tmux scrollback cannot hold it.
#   env               the variable the vendor documents (ANTHROPIC_AUTH_TOKEN, or
#                     ANTHROPIC_API_KEY for Kimi Code); set
#                     WOLFMUX_<PROVIDER>_AUTH_MODE=env in ~/.config/wolfmux/config only as a
#                     last resort, for an endpoint that refuses helper-mode headers: it cannot
#                     fix a wrong key (teamctl doctor --probe says whether the key is accepted),
#                     and for ANTHROPIC_API_KEY Claude Code asks interactively before using it.
# In both modes an inert guard value keeps your claude.ai login away from anything
# the worker spawns (see WOLFMUX_GLM_GUARD_TOKEN in lib/provider-env.sh). This
# launcher refuses to start without it.
#
# A provider billed per token (PROVIDER_BILLING=metered) is refused unless the OWNER's
# ~/.config/wolfmux/config carries WOLFMUX_METERED=on. That file and nothing else: not a
# variable (a pane's environment comes from the tmux server, not from the owner) and not
# a config directory chosen by $WOLFMUX_HOME (an agent sets that). See
# wolfmux_owner_config in lib/providers.sh, which also says what this is not.
#
# Settings (environment, else ~/.config/wolfmux/config), <P> being the provider in
# capitals:
#   WOLFMUX_<P>_AUTH_MODE  helper | env
#   WOLFMUX_<P>_CONTEXT    the window to declare, in tokens; WOLFMUX_GLM_CONTEXT=1m
#                          additionally asks Z.ai for its 1M window (uses quota faster)
#   WOLFMUX_<P>_MODEL      pin the main model id; WOLFMUX_<P>_FAST_MODEL the haiku
#                          tier (both ignored for glm: the plan covers two ids)
#   WOLFMUX_METERED=on     allow a provider billed per token. The owner's own config
#                          file only, located through the account rather than through
#                          $HOME or $WOLFMUX_HOME: neither the environment nor a config
#                          directory an agent chose opens that gate
#   WOLFMUX_CLAUDE_BIN     explicit path to the claude binary
#   WOLFMUX_DRY_RUN=1      print what would run (no secrets) and exit
#   WOLFMUX_EXTRA_SETTINGS per-agent Claude Code settings file, set by teamctl
# ~/.config/wolfmux/glm-worker-settings.json, when present, is a Claude Code settings
# overlay for third-party workers only (default: turns off claude-mem there).
set -euo pipefail

SELF="$(basename "$0")"
WOLFMUX_HOME="${WOLFMUX_HOME:-$HOME/.config/wolfmux}"
LIB="$WOLFMUX_HOME/lib/provider-env.sh"
if [ ! -r "$LIB" ]; then
  echo "$SELF: missing $LIB — refusing to launch without environment scrubbing" >&2
  exit 78
fi
# shellcheck source=/dev/null
. "$LIB"
wolfmux_load_config

# Which row, and which tier of it, this name stands for.
PROVIDER_AND_VARIANT="$(wolfmux_provider_of_launcher "$SELF")" || {
  echo "$SELF: not a provider launcher name. Install one of: $(wolfmux_provider_launcher_names)" >&2
  exit 64
}
PROVIDER="${PROVIDER_AND_VARIANT%% *}"
VARIANT="${PROVIDER_AND_VARIANT##* }"
wolfmux_provider_info "$PROVIDER" || {
  echo "$SELF: no row for provider '$PROVIDER' in lib/providers.sh" >&2
  exit 64
}
UP="$(printf '%s' "$PROVIDER" | tr '[:lower:]' '[:upper:]')"

SCRUBBED="$(wolfmux_list_set_vars "$WOLFMUX_CLAUDE_PROVIDER_VARS $WOLFMUX_CLAUDE_THIRD_PARTY_VARS" "$WOLFMUX_CLAUDE_PROVIDER_PREFIXES" | tr '\n' ' ')"
wolfmux_scrub_claude_env "$WOLFMUX_CLAUDE_THIRD_PARTY_VARS"

CLAUDE_BIN="$(wolfmux_resolve_claude)" || {
  echo "$SELF: Claude Code CLI not found. Install: https://code.claude.com/docs/en/setup" >&2
  exit 127
}

# Housekeeping subcommands (doctor, update, mcp, ...) never talk to a model.
if wolfmux_is_claude_subcommand "${1:-}"; then
  exec "$CLAUDE_BIN" "$@"
fi

AUTH_MODE="$(wolfmux_provider_setting "$PROVIDER" AUTH_MODE)"
AUTH_MODE="${AUTH_MODE:-helper}"
case "$AUTH_MODE" in
  helper | env) ;;
  *)
    echo "$SELF: WOLFMUX_${UP}_AUTH_MODE must be 'helper' or 'env' (got '$AUTH_MODE')" >&2
    exit 64
    ;;
esac

# Claude Code does not know these model ids, so it assumes a 200k window and says so in a
# long yellow notice in every pane. Declaring the provider's real window keeps the
# behaviour and drops the notice (measured against the real CLI; see docs/VERIFICATION.md).
# A model id carrying the [1m] suffix already tells it, and then the number belongs to
# CLAUDE_CODE_AUTO_COMPACT_WINDOW instead. Both variables are on the scrub list on purpose
# (a Fable child must never inherit a provider's window), so the owner's own number goes
# through WOLFMUX_<P>_CONTEXT.
CONTEXT_SET="$(wolfmux_provider_setting "$PROVIDER" CONTEXT)"
SUFFIX=""
GLM_1M=0
CONTEXT_FROM=""
case "$PROVIDER:$CONTEXT_SET" in
  glm:1m)
    # Z.ai sells its 1M window as a model-id suffix, and it spends plan quota faster.
    SUFFIX="[1m]"
    WINDOW="1000000"
    GLM_1M=1
    ;;
  *)
    case "$CONTEXT_SET" in
      "" | *[!0-9]*)
        if [ -n "$CONTEXT_SET" ]; then
          if [ "$PROVIDER" = glm ]; then
            echo "$SELF: WOLFMUX_${UP}_CONTEXT must be '1m' or a number of tokens (got '$CONTEXT_SET'); using $PROVIDER_CONTEXT" >&2
          else
            echo "$SELF: WOLFMUX_${UP}_CONTEXT must be a number of tokens (got '$CONTEXT_SET'); using $PROVIDER_CONTEXT" >&2
          fi
        fi
        WINDOW="$PROVIDER_CONTEXT"
        if [ "$PROVIDER" = glm ]; then
          CONTEXT_FROM="declared; WOLFMUX_GLM_CONTEXT=1m for the 1M window"
        else
          CONTEXT_FROM="declared; WOLFMUX_${UP}_CONTEXT to change it"
        fi
        ;;
      *)
        WINDOW="$CONTEXT_SET"
        CONTEXT_FROM="declared by WOLFMUX_${UP}_CONTEXT"
        ;;
    esac
    ;;
esac

MAIN="$PROVIDER_MAIN_MODEL"
FAST="$PROVIDER_FAST_MODEL"
if [ "$PROVIDER_PINNABLE" = 1 ]; then
  PINNED="$(wolfmux_provider_setting "$PROVIDER" MODEL)"
  [ -z "$PINNED" ] || MAIN="$PINNED"
  PINNED="$(wolfmux_provider_setting "$PROVIDER" FAST_MODEL)"
  [ -z "$PINNED" ] || FAST="$PINNED"
  # `--model <id>` on the command line is how teamctl passes <provider>:<id>. It is the
  # model the session will run on, so it has to decide the mappings and the window too,
  # not just be forwarded: an id without [1m] needs a max-context window even when the
  # table's default id has the suffix, and the other way round. The fast tier keeps the
  # table's id (the caller chose one model, not two).
  ARG_MODEL="$(wolfmux_args_model_value "$@")" || ARG_MODEL=""
  [ -z "$ARG_MODEL" ] || MAIN="$ARG_MODEL"
fi
MAIN="${MAIN}${SUFFIX}"
FAST="${FAST}${SUFFIX}"
case "$VARIANT" in
  fast) PRIMARY="$FAST" ;;
  *) PRIMARY="$MAIN" ;;
esac

# Which variable carries the number depends on the model id, so this waits until the
# id is known: a [1m] id already tells Claude Code the window, and then the number is
# the point at which it starts compacting.
case "$PRIMARY" in
  *'[1m]')
    export CLAUDE_CODE_AUTO_COMPACT_WINDOW="$WINDOW"
    # Read back, not repeated: the line below then reports the number the environment
    # really carries (the same reason the login guard line is read back).
    DECLARED="${CLAUDE_CODE_AUTO_COMPACT_WINDOW:-}"
    if [ "$GLM_1M" = 1 ]; then
      CONTEXT_NOTE="1M ([1m] suffix)"
      [ -n "$DECLARED" ] || CONTEXT_NOTE="NOT DECLARED ([1m] suffix)"
    else
      CONTEXT_NOTE="${DECLARED:-NOT DECLARED} tokens (auto-compact window, the model id carries [1m]; $CONTEXT_FROM)"
    fi
    ;;
  *)
    export CLAUDE_CODE_MAX_CONTEXT_TOKENS="$WINDOW"
    DECLARED="${CLAUDE_CODE_MAX_CONTEXT_TOKENS:-}"
    CONTEXT_NOTE="${DECLARED:-NOT DECLARED} tokens ($CONTEXT_FROM)"
    ;;
esac

export ANTHROPIC_BASE_URL="$PROVIDER_BASE_URL"
export ANTHROPIC_MODEL="$PRIMARY"
export ANTHROPIC_DEFAULT_OPUS_MODEL="$MAIN"
export ANTHROPIC_DEFAULT_SONNET_MODEL="$MAIN"
export ANTHROPIC_DEFAULT_FABLE_MODEL="$MAIN"
export ANTHROPIC_DEFAULT_HAIKU_MODEL="$FAST"
export CLAUDE_CODE_SUBAGENT_MODEL="$MAIN"
export API_TIMEOUT_MS="3000000"
export CLAUDE_CODE_DISABLE_NONESSENTIAL_TRAFFIC="1"
export CLAUDE_CODE_OAUTH_TOKEN="$WOLFMUX_GLM_GUARD_TOKEN"

# What the vendor's own Claude Code guide asks for, after the scrub so a value inherited
# from elsewhere cannot survive. Every name here is on the scrub list, so a Claude
# subscription child of this worker does not inherit it either.
if [ -n "$PROVIDER_EXTRA_ENV" ]; then
  for pair in $PROVIDER_EXTRA_ENV; do
    export "${pair%%=*}=${pair#*=}"
  done
fi

# Billed per token: the owner decides, never an agent, and only in the config file.
# The gate is checked before the Keychain, so the refusal says which of the two
# problems it is.
# The one file that decides, named in full wherever this launcher mentions it.
OWNER_CONFIG="$(wolfmux_owner_config)" || OWNER_CONFIG=""
[ -n "$OWNER_CONFIG" ] || OWNER_CONFIG="$HOME/.config/wolfmux/config (your account has no home directory: guessing)"
METERED_GATE=""
if [ "$PROVIDER_BILLING" = "metered" ]; then
  if wolfmux_metered_on; then
    METERED_GATE="open (WOLFMUX_METERED=on in $OWNER_CONFIG)"
  else
    METERED_GATE="closed"
  fi
fi

KEY_CMD="/usr/bin/security find-generic-password -s ${PROVIDER_KEYCHAIN} -w"
OVERLAY="$WOLFMUX_HOME/glm-worker-settings.json"

# One --settings value: the worker overlay, then the per-agent settings teamctl
# generated for this pane (they win), plus the key helper in helper mode.
HELPER=""
if [ "$AUTH_MODE" = "helper" ]; then HELPER="$KEY_CMD"; fi
SETTINGS_JSON="$(wolfmux_merge_settings "$HELPER" "$OVERLAY" "${WOLFMUX_EXTRA_SETTINGS:-}")" || exit 78

CMD=("$CLAUDE_BIN")
if [ "$SETTINGS_JSON" != "{}" ]; then
  CMD+=(--settings "$SETTINGS_JSON")
fi
if ! wolfmux_args_have_model "$@"; then
  CMD+=(--model "$PRIMARY")
fi
CMD+=("$@")

# The guard is the one export that must never be missing, so it is read back rather than
# assumed: this reports the environment that is actually there, in dry run and for real.
GUARD_NOTE="OFF"
if [ "${CLAUDE_CODE_OAUTH_TOKEN:-}" = "$WOLFMUX_GLM_GUARD_TOKEN" ]; then
  GUARD_NOTE="on (children can never present your claude.ai login to ${PROVIDER_VENDOR%% *})"
fi

# Read back for the same reason: the line then says what the environment holds, not what
# the table asked for.
EXTRA_NOTE=""
for pair in $PROVIDER_EXTRA_ENV; do
  EXTRA_NAME="${pair%%=*}"
  EXTRA_NOTE="$EXTRA_NOTE $EXTRA_NAME=${!EXTRA_NAME:-(NOT SET)}"
done
EXTRA_NOTE="${EXTRA_NOTE# }"

if [ "${WOLFMUX_DRY_RUN:-}" = "1" ]; then
  echo "launcher:        $SELF"
  echo "provider:        $PROVIDER ($PROVIDER_VENDOR)"
  case "$PROVIDER_BILLING" in
    metered) echo "billing:         METERED: $PROVIDER_BILLING_NOTE" ;;
    *) echo "billing:         plan: $PROVIDER_BILLING_NOTE" ;;
  esac
  [ -z "$METERED_GATE" ] || echo "metered gate:    $METERED_GATE"
  echo "endpoint:        $ANTHROPIC_BASE_URL"
  echo "model:           ${ANTHROPIC_MODEL:-NOT SET}   (haiku/background tier: ${ANTHROPIC_DEFAULT_HAIKU_MODEL:-NOT SET})"
  echo "context window:  $CONTEXT_NOTE"
  echo "auth mode:       $AUTH_MODE   (key source: macOS Keychain service '${PROVIDER_KEYCHAIN}')"
  if wolfmux_provider_key_exists "$PROVIDER"; then echo "keychain item:   present"; else echo "keychain item:   MISSING"; fi
  [ -z "$EXTRA_NOTE" ] || echo "extra env:       $EXTRA_NOTE"
  echo "login guard:     $GUARD_NOTE"
  if [ -r "$OVERLAY" ]; then echo "overlay:         $OVERLAY"; else echo "overlay:         none"; fi
  echo "agent settings:  ${WOLFMUX_EXTRA_SETTINGS:-none (not started by teamctl)}"
  echo "scrubbed vars:   ${SCRUBBED:-(none were set)}"
  printf 'would exec:     '
  printf ' %q' "${CMD[@]}"
  echo
  [ "$GUARD_NOTE" != "OFF" ] || exit 78
  exit 0
fi

if [ "$GUARD_NOTE" = "OFF" ]; then
  echo "$SELF: the login guard is not in this process: refusing to launch (a child could present your claude.ai login to ${PROVIDER_VENDOR%% *})" >&2
  exit 78
fi

if [ "$METERED_GATE" = "closed" ]; then
  {
    echo "$SELF: $PROVIDER is billed per token ($PROVIDER_BILLING_NOTE), and the meter is closed."
    echo
    echo "Only you can open it, not an agent, and only in your own config file. Add"
    echo "this line to $OWNER_CONFIG:"
    echo
    echo "  WOLFMUX_METERED=on"
    echo
    echo "Nothing else opens it: not a variable in the environment, and not a config file"
    echo "somewhere else. That file is found through your account, not through \$HOME or"
    echo "\$WOLFMUX_HOME, so an agent cannot point the decision at a file it wrote itself."
    echo
  } >&2
  exit 78
fi

if ! wolfmux_provider_key_exists "$PROVIDER"; then
  {
    echo "$SELF: no Keychain item for service '${PROVIDER_KEYCHAIN}'."
    echo
    wolfmux_provider_key_help "$PROVIDER"
  } >&2
  exit 78
fi

if [ "$AUTH_MODE" = "env" ]; then
  KEY_VALUE="$($KEY_CMD)" || {
    echo "$SELF: could not read the Keychain item (is the login keychain unlocked?)" >&2
    exit 78
  }
  [ -n "$KEY_VALUE" ] || {
    echo "$SELF: Keychain item is empty" >&2
    exit 78
  }
  export "$PROVIDER_AUTH_VAR=$KEY_VALUE"
  unset KEY_VALUE
fi

exec "${CMD[@]}"
